[Options]

[A.]
<h2>Rain</h2>
<i>~I"My best piece of advice for aspiring young priests? Don't get captured!<br>
--CodMackerel, Priest of rain.</i>
<p>You wake up slowly. It is the day of the trial. You try to think what has happened but your mind is clouded over. 
Memories slowly begin to seep through the mist. You remember the sudden arrival of an emissary of the Lord of Rain - no, wait - there were others too. 
What was it they said? Something about a fight to end all fights....if you seek peace, prepare for war.....yes.....something like that - but hadn't they then attacked? 
You struggle to remember what had happened...a vague recollection of the words of your high priest "War stops only peace" he had said "Do you not see? One fury cannot reign supreme!"
 he had screamed at them. Your shudder as you remember the reply "All must die who do not fight for the rain alliance"
the emissary had sneered. The next thing you recall is your pleading for your life as your fellow nimbians were slaughtered without quarter. As one of the trainee priests you plead your worth, if only your life be spared. Much to your relief, 
they had spared you, and today is the day of your trial. You remember not why, but the Lord of Rain himself is watching your trial, perhaps the omnipotent fury of rain has spared
your life for a reason..........

$Button=Play Mission,DoNothing,0

[@25]
<$PlaySound,ourPriestImmobile.wav>
[@28]
hehe, not really. Your priest is fine- for the moment.........
[@380]
<$Config,vn_speed=0>

[Succeeded][BadTeamDead]
<p>Victory!
You have survived. The Lord of Rain is pleased with your performance, you are formally accepted into the Rain alliance, and as a reward
for surviving your initiation, your sun cannon is replaced with an ~lICE CANNON
$Menu= ~[IrainCannon.1],Tell,finish

[finish]
~I"Well done" ~.says the Lord of Rain ~I"You have great potential <?{vn_speed}>, you work fast and efficiently."  "I am sure I can find you a very rewarding role in the quest for Domination of Rain" </?><?!{vn_speed}>, however you were a little slower than I had hoped....nevertheless, I have an important job for you. Come .........."</?></p>
<p>
